+/// ([`Runtime::find_all_services`]) to report services that belong to different interfaces.
+///
+/// # Observed native identity
+/// Every field is an owned, concrete value observed from the native service discovery layer:
+/// the configured service type name, its full [`ServiceVersion`], the binding name, the
+/// binding-specific service id and the binding-specific instance id. There is deliberately no
+/// [`InstanceSpecifier`] here: a FindAny/wildcard result is identified by the native instance id
+/// and not by a consumer-configured specifier, and inventing a specifier for such a result would
+/// be incorrect.
